EmailTemplate.textOnly:
Hello {!Contact.FirstName},

Thank you for applying to Arizona State University. Because you did not meet university minimum admission requirements, your application for admission is denied. An option you may consider is attending one of the many community colleges located near ASU and then transferring to ASU after you receive 24 credits (1 year) and a minimum 2.50 GPA. View admission requirements at https://students.asu.edu/international/future/undergrad#benefits.

The MAPP (Maricopa - ASU Pathways Program) outlines classes for you to take at a local community college to prepare you for your desired degree at ASU. These courses satisfy all lower-division course work required for the selected ASU major and guarantee your admission to ASU upon completion of the associate's degree. Learn more at https://transfer.asu.edu/agreement2/maricopa-county-community-college-district/mapp/.

If you are interested in this program, you can sign up for a MAPP with a community college advisor. I can assist you in transferring to ASU when you are ready.

If you have any questions, please feel free to contact me.

Sincerely,

{!User.Recruiter_Full_Name__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Title__c}
Admission Services
{!User.Recruiter_Email__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Phone__c}

If you have any additional information or questions related to this, please reply to this email.

{!Case.Thread_Id}
